title: 'The processed requests: =(editRequest (processed ...))='
pid: 0a226a39-0aa4-49e3-8f42-269ce1b8acfb
body: |2-
  =(processed OBJECT...)= and =(unprocessed OBJECT...)= inside =(editRequest
  ...)= ask the save to set or clear the processed marks of the
  leaves those objects name. On a vognode or ghost, =rel= names the
  existence of its relationship to its viewparent, and =node= every
  leaf its node records but the relationships shown on it or under it:
  its own relationship to its viewparent, that of each member drawn
  under it (in its content or in a partner folder), whatever its
  aspect, and the content relationships a changeset marker under it
  gathers. So on a new or deleted node =node= names its existence, and
  on a modified node its text, home skgrepo, aliases, extra IDs and
  flags, with any relationship it records that no headline under it
  shows; never its children's containment where the children are
  drawn. On a changeset marker, =rel= names the relationships it
  gathers and =node= the own leaves (existence, text, home skgrepo,
  aliases, extra IDs, flags) of their members, one level down. With no
  object a request names what =(leaves ...)= can list: =node= and =rel=
  on a vognode, =rel= on a changeset marker or an unknown viewnode, and
  the one leaf elsewhere. There is no object =all=; a request naming it
  is refused as an unknown diff object. On a vognode, the objects =newContent=
  and =newOutward= name leaves of the new nodes a walk reaches from its
  node, through new nodes only: the node itself when it is new, and
  each new member of a relationship the walk follows that a node
  reached records ('ChangeLeaves::new_nodes_reached_from').
  =newContent= follows content relationships, and names each new node's
  existence (which covers its text) and its content relationships;
  =newOutward= follows every relationship in its recorded direction,
  and names every leaf each new node records
  ('ChangeLeaves::leaves_of_new_nodes_reached_from', 'NewNodeWalk').
  Neither names the relationship of the node to its container. Beside
  a walk, =node= and =rel= also filter what it reaches: =node= names
  each new node's existence, =rel= the relationships it records that
  the walk follows, and a walk with neither names both:
  =(processed rel newContent)= marks the headline's relationship to its
  viewparent and the content relationships of the new nodes reached. The
  server reads all this from the change forest; what the buffer shows,
  or write-protects, does not matter. No change fact lists either
  object. Since which leaves they name only the change forest can
  tell, validation takes such a request to share a leaf with every
  request of the opposite kind in the same save that can name a leaf of
  the same kind (a node's own, or a relationship), and refuses the
  save; likewise =node= on a changeset marker, with every request that
  can name an own leaf of a content member drawn beside it. At most one per headline, written after
  the headline's other edit request if it has one: =(editRequest
  delete (processed node))=. Any headline that may carry =(diff ...)= may
  carry one.
